Merge summary
The one file that actually changed: src/softmac_platform_android.c

The NetHunter module's platform file was the superset (Modes A/B/C/D, CTW-11, dual TUN, routing). The AoA platform file was the earlier simpler version. The merge takes the NetHunter version as base and brings in two things from AoA:

From AoA: Per-path EACCES advisory in open_tun(). The NetHunter version silently discarded the error. The AoA version printed a specific fix for the operator (setenforce 0, ro.boot.selinux=permissive, Echoe ROM note) per path — that's genuinely useful diagnostics and was restored.

Fixed: ratchet_cipher_init() — the NetHunter file called it with 5 args; AoA's ratchet_cipher.h declares 4. The 5th arg (mn, monotonic sec) was redundant because seed_time in usb_sync_params_t already captures the connection epoch. Reduced to 4 args. ratchet_cipher.c is byte-for-byte untouched.
